<title>SWITZERLAND: SBC says Dillon buy creates no overlaps.</title>
<headline>SBC says Dillon buy creates no overlaps.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>SBC Warburg's acquisition of U.S. investment bank Dillon Read &amp; Co would combine two complementary operations and not result in any business overlaps, Swiss Bank Corp Chief Executive Marcel Ospel said.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't expect any problems whatsoever...there aren't any overlaps,&quot; Ospel told Reuters said in a telephone interview.</p>
<p>He also said the $600 million price being paid for Dillon Read is justified given the values the merger would create.</p>
</text>
